WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.879
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 2, Network implementation, which is 20 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:10.485
This lesson covers objective 2 point 3.

00:00:10.485 --> 00:00:15.362
Given a scenario, select and configure wireless devices and technologies.

00:00:15.362 --> 00:00:20.640
Today's concept: the wireless security protocols and what each one is built on.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.223
WEP is the oldest.

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:30.626
It used the RC4 cipher with a short initialization vector, and it can be cracked in minutes.

00:00:30.626 --> 00:00:31.670
It is obsolete.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.940
WPA2 replaced RC4 with AES, running in CCMP mode.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:43.570
WPA3 replaces the pre shared key handshake with simultaneous authentication of equals, or SAE.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:48.958
SAE matters because each password guess needs a live, rate limited exchange.

00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:55.310
That stops offline guessing of a captured four way handshake, which works against WPA2 Personal.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.518
Enterprise mode is different.

00:00:57.518 --> 00:01:03.570
It authenticates each user through a RADIUS server with 802.1X, instead of one shared password.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:08.810
And the WPS setup PIN is vulnerable to brute force, so turn it off.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.349
For the exam, WEP is RC4 and obsolete.

00:01:14.349 --> 00:01:16.190
WPA2 is AES with CCMP.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:24.389
WPA3 swaps the shared-key handshake for SAE, and enterprise mode adds 802.1X with a RADIUS server.

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:27.150
That's objective two point three.
